# TaskProX — all variables are OPTIONAL. The defaults point at the existing production Firebase project.
# Firebase web config is public by design (security comes from firestore.rules / storage.rules), but it can be
# overridden to point a build at a different Firebase project (e.g. staging):
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID=

# Test builds only (set by `npm run build:e2e`). NEVER set this for a production build:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_USE_FIREBASE_EMULATORS=1

# Test tooling only: use an already-installed Chromium for Playwright.
# PW_CHROMIUM_PATH=/path/to/chromium

# scripts/migrate-legacy-data.mjs only (never shipped to the browser):
# GCLOUD_PROJECT=taskprox-58458
# GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=/absolute/path/to/service-account.json   # keep OUT of git
